⚡ PERFORMANCE TIPS: Building Faster, Smarter Anaplan Models
  - This guide provides proven strategies to optimize Anaplan model performance, from formula design to model architecture, 
    helping you reduce calculation times, avoid workspace limits, and improve end-user experience

🧠 CORE PRINCIPLES
  - Minimize Model Size
  - Reduce Calculation Complexity
  - Control Dimensionality
  - Use Booleans & Conditional Logic Wisely
  - Avoid Repeating Calculations
  - Benchmark & Monitor

🚧 1. MODEL DESIGN DOs & DON'Ts
  ✅ Do  |  🚫 Don’t
  Use flat lists and system modules for properties  |  Store properties directly in lists
  Normalize inputs in the Data Hub  |  Normalize/transform in the spoke
  Use Line Item Subsets for conditional logic  |  Create separate line items per logic block
  Keep calculations modular and clean  |  Create long chained formulas
  Set summary methods to 'None' by default  |  Leave summaries on unnecessarily

🔬 2. FORMULA OPTIMIZATION
  ✅ Best Practices
    - Split complex logic into intermediate line items
    - Reuse line items to avoid recalculating the same formula
    - Place IF statements early to short-circuit logic:
      > IF NOT Active? THEN 0 ELSE Long_Formula
    - Use Booleans for filtering & visibility logic instead of IF THEN ELSE
    - Avoid formulas referencing multiple large modules with different dimensions

🚨 Watch Out For:
  - TEXT(), FIND(), and SEARCH() functions — memory intensive
  - Circular references
  - Excessive use of SELECT, LOOKUP, SUM in a single formula

🧮 3. DIMENSIONS & SPARSITY CONTROL
  Optimization Area  | 	Tip
  Dimensionality  |  Avoid over-dimensioning; don’t mix unrelated dimensions
  Time  |  Use Time Ranges to limit scope
  Users List  |  Keep as small as possible (applies to DCA)
  Versioning  |  Use switchover + fake version logic when applicable

⛔ 4. SUMMARY METHODS
  Line Item Type  |  Default Summary
  Number  |  None unless needed
  Boolean  |  ANY, ALL if needed, else None
  Text  |  None (avoid summarizing text)
  -- Rule: Turn off summary methods unless explicitly required for dashboards or exports

📤 5. DATA IMPORTS & EXPORTS
  - Use code-based imports (faster + more stable than name-based)
  - Avoid importing from views with filters or large dimensions
  - Turn off summary methods in import source modules
  - Use simple views for exports (only needed line items and rows)

🔄 6. CALCULATION ENGINE TIPS
  - Avoid volatile logic across many cells (especially in large grids)
  - Trigger recalculations via booleans instead of data cell changes
  - Schedule batch jobs during off-hours to reduce user latency
  - Keep data flows one-directional (e.g., Data Hub → Spoke)

📊 7. DASHBOARD/UX PERFORMANCE
  Best Practice 	|  Why
  Keep cards lightweight (limit rows/columns)  |  Faster load/render time
  Avoid dynamic selectors on massive lists  |  Can stall user interaction
  Pre-filter views in modules  |  Less UI burden on filter logic
  Use linked navigation instead of nested pages  |  Reduces load chaining

🧩 8. ADVANCED STRATEGIES
  - Use calculation scoping (custom booleans to limit formula triggers)
  - Build aggregation layers (e.g., summarize region totals in one module, reuse across others)
  - Use fake versions to simulate scenario planning without full versioning overhead
  - Periodically archive or delete unused data (historical snapshots, staging lists)

📈 9. TESTING & MONITORING TOOLS
  Tool  |  Usage
  Model Open Time  |  Monitor initial load size/performance
  Model Map  |  Identify dependency chains and bottlenecks
  Cell Count Viewer  |  Gauge module bloat
  History Log  |  Identify recent changes impacting performance
  Workspace Size  |  Monitor near-limit usage (10GB+ flags risk)

✅ 10. PERFORMANCE CHECKLIST
  ✅ Check	Description
    🔲 Line items summarized only where needed	
    🔲 Avoided nested IF THEN ELSE chains	
    🔲 Time Ranges applied to all applicable modules	
    🔲 Boolean line items used for filters and triggers	
    🔲 Text and list formatting minimized in core logic	
    🔲 Formulas are broken down for reuse/modularity	
    🔲 Imports/exports are fast and cleanly structured	
